Good. That means you can do some setup before getting started. I use the
setup that the Pudding Farmbot uses. You can find it here:

http://scavenger.homeip.net/autohack/Farmbot

I usually also block squares B5 and D5 but you may get better pudding
flow if you leave them open.

Next scour the level and make sure that all hole and level teleports
are plugged. It's a real bummer when you realize that there are puddings
flowing down 3-5 levels below your current location.

Use a wand of digging or a pickaxe to chisel as much of the level as you
can. If you have poly control and an amulet of unchanging, a perfect combo
for this is turning into an umber hulk and put on the amulet. You can chew
out an entire level in about 2000 turns. And the rock makes you full.

>
>I don't have a stethoscope, so I'll wait a while. This could be fun. Or
>not.

You don't have to have the stethescope. I simply name my puddings with turn
numbers before I split them. Any pudding that is less than 500 turns old goes
unsplit. I use detect monsters to see how full the level is. Once it's full
just whack away with a metal object. You never kill more than you split.

Good luck.

